1
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:09,170
Imagine walking into a company where every team spins up

2
00:00:09,289 --> 00:00:11,850
Google Cloud projects however they want,

3
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:16,059
no structure, no rules, and definitely no consistency.

4
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:21,469
That's exactly why Google Cloud organizations exists, to bring the control,

5
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:25,649
order, and structure to everything that happens in your environment.

6
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,760
Let's understand it in more detail.

7
00:00:27,809 --> 00:00:32,819
You can think of the Google Cloud organization as the org nod, as the top

8
00:00:32,819 --> 00:00:37,790
level container that represents your entire company inside the Google Cloud.

9
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:41,259
It is kind of a root folder on your computer,

10
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:44,619
except it is something that controls the identity,

11
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:48,380
security, IAM policies, billing, resource planning,

12
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:49,040
everything.

13
00:00:49,139 --> 00:00:54,060
The official document describes it as the root node in the Google Cloud

14
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:59,590
resource hierarchy that defines the administrative boundary for all resources

15
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:03,090
in the organization. So if someone creates a project,

16
00:01:03,279 --> 00:01:04,888
it belongs to the organization.

17
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:08,900
If you create a folder, that will also go inside the organization.

18
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,190
Policies, that is also inside the organization,

19
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:14,930
and the resource all eventually belongs to the organization.

20
00:01:15,089 --> 00:01:18,290
Organization is important to have the consistency.

21
00:01:18,379 --> 00:01:21,889
Let's say, imagine you are an admin at a global company.

22
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:25,370
You want all the new resources like every virtual machine,

23
00:01:25,599 --> 00:01:26,389
every bucket,

24
00:01:26,769 --> 00:01:31,345
every service to follow certain rules like only allowed region possible,

25
00:01:31,544 --> 00:01:35,214
no public IPs, shielded VMs, and CMEK required.

26
00:01:35,535 --> 00:01:37,665
Now if you don't have the organization node,

27
00:01:37,745 --> 00:01:42,305
you have to keep setting those rules manually for every new project,

28
00:01:42,495 --> 00:01:44,464
and developers could easily overwrite them.

29
00:01:44,584 --> 00:01:46,175
But with the Google Cloud organization,

30
00:01:46,745 --> 00:01:50,084
you set them once using organization policies,

31
00:01:50,105 --> 00:01:52,264
and they cascade automatically.

32
00:01:52,385 --> 00:01:57,019
Another huge benefit of organization node is the identity control.

33
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:59,680
Your entire cloud environment can be bound to

34
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,110
Google Workspace or Cloud Identity.

35
00:02:02,279 --> 00:02:07,559
This means users don't create the random Google account to access the resources.

36
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:11,199
You control the identity from a single place,

37
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:14,679
the same place your company manages email,

38
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,610
devices, and groups.

39
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:20,520
Enterprise IAM rules also start at the organization level.

40
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:23,934
You can set organization admins, security admins,

41
00:02:24,335 --> 00:02:27,764
networking admins, and those permissions flow downwards.

42
00:02:27,774 --> 00:02:30,975
You can think of organization as a headquarter,

43
00:02:31,134 --> 00:02:34,975
folders like a department, projects like an application,

44
00:02:35,104 --> 00:02:38,115
and resources are like your virtual machine,

45
00:02:38,535 --> 00:02:42,975
instances, clusters, databases, APIs, etc.

46
00:02:43,214 --> 00:02:46,244
You would not run a company without a structure,

47
00:02:46,365 --> 00:02:49,414
and you should not run Cloud without it either.
